Chapter: BlockSelectDrives

 Two disks are attached: 128 sectors whose first bytes are A1 A2 A3 on the
 primary master, and 256 sectors whose first bytes are B1 B2 B3 on the slave.
 The sizes differ and the contents differ, and both differences are load
 bearing.

 block-select did nothing at all until 2026-07-27. It wrote three cells --
 ata-active-drive-addr, ata-active-base-addr, ata-active-select-addr -- that no
 other code in the compiler read, while emit-ata-setup-lba put the literal 224
 on the drive-head port before every read and every write. So every block
 operation in the system went to the primary master whatever the caller
 selected. block-sector-count was worse than inert: it returned a cell written
 once at boot for whichever drive was probed then, so every drive reported
 drive 0's geometry.

 Neither could be seen, because every test in the tree attached at most one
 disk, and with one image behind every position a working selector and a
 missing one produce identical output. That is the shape this project keeps
 writing down: a function that always answers the same thing looks exactly like
 one that works.

 So this test demands four things a single disk cannot produce. Drive 0 must
 answer 128 and A1; drive 1 must answer 256 and B1, which is a different size
 AND different content, so neither a stale count nor a stale channel can pass;
 and drives 2 and 3, on a channel with nothing on it, must answer zero sectors
 rather than inheriting the last drive's count. The floating bus reads back as
 255 on an absent position, and that is the reading, not a placeholder.

 We say:

Section: Body

  report-drive : Integer -> [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  report-drive (i) = act
    w <- block-select i
    n <- block-sector-count
    buf <- block-read-sector 0
    print-line-uni ("drive " & show i & " sectors " & show n
      & " lba0 " & show (peek-byte buf 0))
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    report-drive 0
    report-drive 1
    report-drive 2
    report-drive 3
  end
